    "title": "pandas.Timedelta.unit — pandas 3.1.0.dev0 documentation",
    "status": 200,
    "markdown": "# pandas.Timedelta.unit#\n\n- Timedelta.unit#\n- Return the unit of Timedelta object. The unit of Timedelta object is nanosecond, i.e., ‘ns’ by default. \n  - Returns:\n    - str\n See also \n  - `Timedelta.value`\n  - Return the value of Timedelta object in nanoseconds.\n  - `Timedelta.as_unit`\n  - Convert the underlying int64 representation to the given unit.\n Examples >>> td = pd.Timedelta(42, unit='us') >>> td.unit 'us'",
    "markdown_length": 418,
